GBDK-2020 4.1.1 (gbdk-2020/gbdk-2020, release 4.1.1, linux64)
  GNU GPL v2 with a linking exception for the GBDK library: linking it into a ROM does not
  by itself put the ROM under the GPL. The notice is THIRD_PARTY_GBDK_LICENSE.txt.
  https://github.com/gbdk-2020/gbdk-2020
  The GBDK runtime and ZGB's prebuilt hUGEDriver object (hUGEDriver is public domain,
  by SuperDisk) are linked into the ROM.

ZGB-Template (Zal0/ZGB-Template, commit 37a5da36e04ed6551ce15cb94804450c3b77c7dc)
  Used only as a structural reference (src/Makefile variables, include/ZGBMain.h
  STATES/SPRITES layout, ZGBMain.c next_state/GetTileReplacement). The
  repository publishes no license file, so no template file or binary asset
  (font.gbr, tiles.gbr, map.gbm, player.gbr) is copied; this project's
  Makefile, headers and sources are written from ZGB's own README and headers
  (ZGB is MIT). The font, background and sprite PNGs are original and are
  generated by tools/gen_assets.py.

Toolchain notes
  GBDK 4.5.0 does not link with ZGB v2023.0 (duplicate symbol .refresh_OAM
  between ZGB's linker flags and GBDK 4.5 crt0), and GBDK 4.0.6 lacks
  sdcc -msm83. GBDK 4.1.1 builds cleanly.
